  "views": {
    "hero": "three_quarter",
    "reads": {
      "front": "Over the shoulder the wave runs away from the camera: rows of spikes burst up one after another into the distance, the far rows bigger even though they are further away, ending in a tall eruption and dust plume around the target.",
      "side": "The escalation reads best here: a staircase of rock rising left to right, small spikes near the caster and towering ones at the far end, debris arcing up and falling, dust rolling along the ground.",
      "top": "The ground story: a fan of fissures and a frontal arc of churned dust sweeping outward from the crater at the caster's feet, rows of rock popping up across a 100 degree arc, debris scattering, then the crumbling. The contracting dust ring shows the wind-up.",
      "three_quarter": "Hero view. The arc reads as a widening fan of rock rising row by row toward the target, the rows clearly growing, debris and dust thrown high, cracks and crater on the ground."
    }
  },
